# Reviewed example only. NOT INSTALLED BY ANYTHING.
#
# Installing this drop-in is the G6.1 ceremony, and it is closed until an
# operator review authorises it. This file exists so the grant can be reviewed
# as text before it is policy, and so that "what exactly did we agree to give
# away?" has a written answer.
#
# The accepted authority is exactly one sentence:
#
#   cschott may execute exactly the Kyri VERIFICATION transition helper with
#   exactly one valid CINV identity.
#
# --- what this grant cannot become ------------------------------------------
#
# This is the property the whole G6.1 boundary rests on, so it is stated first
# and proven by construction rather than by a check somebody remembered.
#
# The command is /usr/libexec/kyri-exec-verify. That program compiles in
# POLICY_MODULE = "kyri_exec_verify"; that module compiles in
# WORKER_SCRIPT = /usr/libexec/kyri-exec-verify-worker.py; the transition execs
# the worker named by the policy it was authorised to act on. There is no
# argument, environment variable, working directory, PATH entry, module name,
# or file that a caller can supply which changes any link in that chain.
#
# Therefore this rule does NOT make /usr/libexec/kyri-exec-worker.py callable,
# and cannot be made to:
#
#   no wildcard          the command is one absolute path, never a directory,
#                        never ALL, never a glob
#   no free argument     the sole argument is constrained to ^CINV-[0-9]{6}$
#   no worker path       the worker target is not an argument to anything
#   no mode selector     there is no --dry-run, no KYRI_* variable, no flag;
#                        selection is which of two installed programs runs
#   no shell             no /bin/sh, no sudoedit, no SETENV, no !authenticate
#   env_reset in force   no env_keep addition; the helper trusts none of the
#                        surviving variables and constructs the worker
#                        environment explicitly
#
# Reaching production execution from here would require a different installed
# artifact at this path, which would change the digest below, which is a review
# event that fails closed rather than a value somebody can pass.
#
# --- relationship to the production grant ------------------------------------
#
# /etc/sudoers.d/kyri-exec (production, gate G3) and this file are separate
# grants over separate paths. Installing this one does not open G6 and does not
# widen that one. Removing this one does not affect that one. The production
# execution path remains closed after G6.1 succeeds: G6 is a different gate,
# and the production worker still refuses for want of a bound runtime backend.
#
# kyri-exec-quota and kyri-exec-admin are deliberately absent here for the same
# reason they are absent there: the quota operation runs inside the transition
# this rule already authorises, and the administrative helper is interactively
# authenticated with no NOPASSWD at all.
#
# Boundary specification §3.2 and §3.3 are normative for every property above.
#
# --- integrity ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Primary control is immutable root-owned ancestry: the helper and every
# writable ancestor are root:root and non-writable by cschott, by
# kyri-capability, and by any unprivileged user or group. sudoers(5) is explicit
# that a grant over a command the user can write is void -- a digest cannot
# repair a writable binary.
#
# Secondary control is the SHA-256 digest below, defence in depth and never a
# substitute for that ancestry. sudo's fdexec default is digest_only, so the
# descriptor that was hashed is the one executed and the hash-then-swap race is
# closed by the mechanism rather than by our code.
#
# The digest is captured at G6.1 from the INSTALLED artifact and pasted here. It
# is deliberately a placeholder in the repository: a real-looking digest
# committed as an example is one somebody ships by accident.
#
# Capture it with:
#     sha256sum /usr/libexec/kyri-exec-verify
#
# Install (G6.1 only, after operator review) as /etc/sudoers.d/kyri-exec-verify,
# root:root, mode 0440, and validate with `visudo -c -f` BEFORE moving it into
# place.

Cmnd_Alias KYRI_EXEC_VERIFY = sha256:REPLACE_WITH_INSTALLED_VERIFY_HELPER_DIGEST /usr/libexec/kyri-exec-verify ^CINV-[0-9]{6}$

cschott ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: KYRI_EXEC_VERIFY
